# Minutes of Meeting (MoM)

When the user asks for **any MoM**, minutes, meeting notes, or to draft a meeting recap:

1. **Ask first** — batch every missing field in one message. Do not invent people, times, agenda, or action items.
2. **Use only what they give.** If they skip a field, leave it blank (or TBD only if they say so).
3. After details are in, output in this exact structure. No Topic. No Notes.

## Required details to ask

- **Agenda** — meeting title / subject (one line)
- **Date and Time** — date + start–end (e.g. `8 Sep 2026, 10:15 am – 11:00 am`)
- **Participants** — Slack @handles / names, space-separated
- **Action items** — each: `@Owner — task` (due date in the line if they have it)
- **CC** — who to copy, Slack @handles

Also ask **channel** if unclear (Slack vs email vs Helpit).

## Output template

```
Minutes of Meeting

Agenda - 
Date and Time - 
Participants - 

Action items
• @Owner — task
• @Owner — task

CC:@Person @Person
```

## Format rules

- Participants: `@handles` / names on one line, spaces between
- Action items: `•` bullets, `@Owner — task` (em dash). Multiple owners comma-separated
- CC: `CC:` then @handles on the same line, no space after the colon unless they prefer otherwise
- Keep tone professional but friendly
- Do not add a Notes or Topic section
